WEBVTT

00:01.543 --> 00:05.464
(August 13, Meiji 5)

00:14.640 --> 00:16.642
The festival hasn't even started yet,

00:16.725 --> 00:18.810
but I'm already feeling excited.

00:25.734 --> 00:28.904
I'm planning to visit the stalls
with Nomari that day.

00:28.987 --> 00:30.531
You're welcome to join us if you want.

00:30.614 --> 00:32.366
Huh? Really?

00:33.325 --> 00:35.410
Awesome! I'm looking forward to it!

00:36.328 --> 00:39.331
Yes. But before that,

00:43.001 --> 00:45.712
we need to do what we came here to do.

00:49.591 --> 00:52.761
Sorry to bother you when you're so busy.

00:52.845 --> 00:54.555
Please don't worry about it.

00:54.638 --> 00:59.226
So you want to talk about
the "Mirror of Sky Fox", right?

00:59.393 --> 01:00.477
Yes.

01:00.561 --> 01:03.397
Based on my investigation of the legend,

01:03.480 --> 01:06.817
for his ailing wife, a young man,
the husband of the celestial maiden,

01:06.900 --> 01:09.736
burned the body
of a talking fox into ashes

01:09.820 --> 01:14.116
and mixed them to forge the mirror.

01:15.158 --> 01:21.290
But don't you think the legend
of the Mirror of Sky Fox is a bit strange?

01:22.249 --> 01:26.086
Supernatural tales are usually
a blend of truth and falsehood,

01:26.170 --> 01:30.299
which later become legends
through word of mouth.

01:30.382 --> 01:33.969
Do you mean there's
some falsehood in this legend?

01:39.210 --> 01:41.800
(Family Prosperity, Wish Fulfillment)

01:53.447 --> 01:58.452
(Sword of the Demon Hunter)

03:14.027 --> 03:16.405
You must be Ms. Asagao, right?

03:16.488 --> 03:17.698
Y-Yes.

03:18.115 --> 03:20.200
Do you like festivals?

03:20.951 --> 03:21.994
Yes.

03:22.077 --> 03:23.912
The festival is coming up, isn't it?

03:24.288 --> 03:29.376
There will be plenty of stalls then.
It's sure to be a lively festival.

03:29.459 --> 03:33.422
Ms. Asagao, is there a food
you're especially fond of?

03:33.505 --> 03:36.425
Well... there are quite a lot.

03:36.508 --> 03:38.802
But candy apples are my favorite.

03:41.597 --> 03:44.099
Candy apples are good.

03:44.183 --> 03:46.018
I like it too.

03:46.768 --> 03:48.103
Really?

03:48.187 --> 03:49.021
Yes.

03:49.104 --> 03:52.482
When I taste them,
I feel like I'm really at a festival.

03:52.566 --> 03:54.276
I know what you mean.

03:54.359 --> 03:58.030
But candy apples
make me feel full after just one.

03:58.113 --> 04:00.490
You're right.

04:00.574 --> 04:03.660
Excuse me, I've brought you some tea.

04:07.247 --> 04:09.041
It's isobe mochi.

04:09.124 --> 04:11.001
Kadono, that's great.

04:11.084 --> 04:12.628
Do you like it?

04:12.711 --> 04:15.130
Please take your time and enjoy it.

04:15.797 --> 04:18.926
Because once my husband starts talking,
he often goes on and on.

04:19.009 --> 04:20.928
I'm really sorry.

04:21.428 --> 04:23.847
Mr. Kadono, Ms. Asagao.

04:23.931 --> 04:25.432
If you don't mind,

04:25.516 --> 04:27.976
would you like me to show you
the Mirror of Sky Fox?

04:28.393 --> 04:29.853
Would that be okay?

04:37.819 --> 04:40.280
This is the Mirror of Sky Fox.

04:40.364 --> 04:43.784
At first glance,
it's just an ordinary iron mirror.

04:44.159 --> 04:48.580
However, in the past, it showed
the power spoken of in the legend.

04:48.664 --> 04:53.001
The power to connect heaven and earth.

04:53.544 --> 04:56.213
So perhaps, it can also traverse time

04:56.296 --> 04:59.758
and send a celestial maiden
back to the distant heavens.

05:00.217 --> 05:01.093
What?

05:01.176 --> 05:03.136
And you are also from a foreign land,

05:03.220 --> 05:05.514
from a place that is very far away.

05:06.056 --> 05:07.349
Am I right?

05:09.184 --> 05:10.727
How do you know...

05:11.061 --> 05:12.855
Because this is the second time.

05:13.689 --> 05:16.441
The trigger condition is blood.

05:16.525 --> 05:19.820
Just drop your blood
on the mirror and touch it.

05:19.903 --> 05:21.196
That way...

05:21.280 --> 05:23.323
you can return to the place you yearn for,

05:23.407 --> 05:26.410
the time you want to return to.

05:30.289 --> 05:31.582
I'm sorry!

05:31.665 --> 05:36.086
Sure enough, I still want
to prepare myself a bit more.

05:37.671 --> 05:39.047
I see.

05:40.465 --> 05:43.343
So you're going to abandon
the feathered robe yourself.

05:46.680 --> 05:50.851
Please come find me
if you need anything else.

05:50.976 --> 05:53.937
(Demon Soba)

05:54.229 --> 05:55.355
And you know what?

05:55.439 --> 05:59.193
Everyone's praising my new yukata.

05:59.985 --> 06:02.571
That yukata is really cute, after all.

06:02.654 --> 06:04.198
And it really suits you.

06:04.281 --> 06:06.658
Father picked it out for me.

06:07.075 --> 06:10.287
As expected of Kadono,
you really know how to choose.

06:10.579 --> 06:12.623
Ms. Asagao, you're coming too, right?

06:13.582 --> 06:15.417
Yes... I am.

06:15.709 --> 06:17.085
I see.

06:17.169 --> 06:18.629
I'm looking forward to it.

06:21.381 --> 06:22.716
Yes.

06:37.105 --> 06:38.440
Kadono?

06:39.316 --> 06:40.651
Did I wake you?

06:40.901 --> 06:43.654
No. I just couldn't sleep.

06:44.112 --> 06:45.531
Come to think of it,

06:45.614 --> 06:47.824
we haven't really sat down and talked.

06:47.908 --> 06:49.660
This might be a good opportunity.

06:49.743 --> 06:53.914
Honestly, I feel like you're
always taking care of me.

06:54.665 --> 06:55.999
Don't worry about it.

06:56.083 --> 06:57.876
Have you gotten used to living here?

06:58.168 --> 06:59.169
Yes.

06:59.503 --> 07:01.380
I was a bit lost at the beginning.

07:01.505 --> 07:03.173
But it's pretty fun once I get used to it.

07:05.884 --> 07:07.177
What's wrong?

07:07.761 --> 07:08.762
Nothing.

07:10.848 --> 07:11.723
Hey...

07:11.807 --> 07:12.724
Yes?

07:12.808 --> 07:15.894
Why were you willing to let me stay here?

07:17.145 --> 07:18.647
At that time too...

07:19.481 --> 07:22.401
No matter how much trouble they're in,

07:22.484 --> 07:25.737
most people wouldn't let
a total stranger stay the night, right?

07:33.412 --> 07:34.955
A long time ago,

07:35.038 --> 07:36.874
when I ran away from home
and had nowhere to go,

07:36.957 --> 07:38.667
I met someone willing to take me in.

07:41.670 --> 07:44.464
Maybe I've always held on to that.

07:44.548 --> 07:48.844
That's why I did something
so out of character.

07:50.554 --> 07:52.764
I have something to ask you too.

07:52.848 --> 07:54.600
Sure, what is it?

07:54.892 --> 07:57.728
Is the place where you come from boring?

08:03.650 --> 08:04.902
Why do you ask?

08:07.613 --> 08:09.948
Looking at you now,

08:10.032 --> 08:11.617
I somehow get that feeling.

08:12.701 --> 08:16.580
It's not exactly boring.

08:16.663 --> 08:18.498
I have friends, after all.

08:19.124 --> 08:22.294
It's just that sometimes
I feel a little tired.

08:23.086 --> 08:25.839
I go to school every day,
sit through classes,

08:25.923 --> 08:28.091
and at the end, head home with my friends.

08:28.175 --> 08:31.220
Along the way, we'll stop by
all sorts of places to hang out.

08:31.762 --> 08:34.014
Every day is really fun.

08:36.391 --> 08:40.521
But sometimes it feels suffocating.

08:41.021 --> 08:43.732
I have a female friend
who's a shrine maiden.

08:43.815 --> 08:45.609
She's very mature.

08:45.692 --> 08:47.861
She found what she wanted
to do at an early age,

08:47.945 --> 08:50.364
and her grades are also better than mine.

08:51.114 --> 08:53.742
And the boy sitting next to me in class,

08:53.825 --> 08:55.536
he's amazing too.

08:55.619 --> 08:58.163
He's strong and kind.

08:58.247 --> 09:02.793
Even though he knows he'll get hurt,
he's still working hard for his goal.

09:04.086 --> 09:06.588
Someone like me
who spends every day just having fun,

09:06.672 --> 09:08.966
what am I even doing?

09:09.883 --> 09:12.135
What's wrong with having fun?

09:12.219 --> 09:14.054
There's nothing wrong with it.

09:14.638 --> 09:15.556
It's just...

09:15.639 --> 09:17.349
I think those who keep pushing forward,

09:17.432 --> 09:20.143
no matter how hard things get,
are more amazing...

09:20.227 --> 09:22.771
while I'm good for nothing.

09:26.191 --> 09:29.528
Kadono, are you happy now?

09:37.870 --> 09:41.039
I think my life now isn't so bad.

09:41.123 --> 09:44.501
But if I'm asked whether I'm happy...

09:44.585 --> 09:46.545
I can't answer.

09:46.628 --> 09:48.672
Because I don't even know if I'm happy.

09:49.798 --> 09:51.675
It's kind of embarrassing to admit.

09:52.509 --> 09:53.760
I see.

09:54.303 --> 09:58.223
When the ordinary days
start to feel heavy,

09:58.307 --> 10:02.144
we all want to slow down
and take a breather.

10:04.771 --> 10:08.192
If that wish comes true by chance,

10:08.275 --> 10:11.153
and one can finally breathe with ease,

10:12.029 --> 10:15.490
one would probably fear going back
to those ordinary days again.

10:22.497 --> 10:24.041
Life never goes the way you wish.

10:25.042 --> 10:28.378
Just living is already hard enough.

10:29.963 --> 10:31.256
But...

10:31.340 --> 10:34.426
You can't just stay stuck
in place like this?

10:35.302 --> 10:36.470
A long time ago,

10:36.553 --> 10:39.139
a boy in my class told me that.

10:39.223 --> 10:41.808
So I actually know it in my heart.

10:41.892 --> 10:44.186
No matter how comfortable I am,

10:44.269 --> 10:46.313
I can't just remain stagnant.

10:47.314 --> 10:49.566
But just a little longer.

10:49.650 --> 10:54.196
Could you let me rest here
a tiny bit longer?

10:55.280 --> 10:58.951
Yes. It's fine to relax once in a while.

10:59.368 --> 11:02.704
Yes, just a bit more rest.

11:05.000 --> 11:09.190
(August 14, Meiji 5)

11:12.589 --> 11:14.675
I'll be going then, Kadono.

11:14.758 --> 11:16.218
Thank you for looking after me.

11:17.219 --> 11:19.638
Take care, Ms. Celestial Maiden.

11:19.721 --> 11:23.100
Gosh, you're joking again.

11:23.517 --> 11:24.560
When I get back,

11:24.643 --> 11:27.396
I won't have the chance
to come here again, right?

11:27.479 --> 11:28.897
Probably.

11:28.981 --> 11:30.858
I'm afraid we won't get
the chance to meet again.

11:33.652 --> 11:35.112
According to legend,

11:35.195 --> 11:36.864
celestial maidens
who returned to the heavens

11:36.947 --> 11:38.907
sometimes come to the human world to play.

11:38.991 --> 11:41.785
But reality could never go that smoothly.

11:42.244 --> 11:43.871
It's a shame,

11:43.954 --> 11:46.582
but this is probably
our last farewell in this life.

11:46.665 --> 11:48.000
Yes.

11:50.085 --> 11:52.171
Did you have a good rest?

11:52.254 --> 11:53.213
Yes.

11:53.297 --> 11:56.341
I feel like I'll be able to work
a little harder when I get back.

11:56.425 --> 11:57.634
What about you?

11:58.010 --> 11:59.386
Still the same.

11:59.469 --> 12:01.054
I don't plan to change anything.

12:01.138 --> 12:03.432
You're so stubborn.

12:03.515 --> 12:04.892
That's a compliment to me.

12:11.773 --> 12:14.526
Well then, I should get going.

12:25.996 --> 12:27.581
I was thinking...

12:27.664 --> 12:30.417
If I were to go to the festival
with you all tomorrow,

12:30.501 --> 12:32.211
then we'd be watching the moon together,

12:32.294 --> 12:34.671
and when winter came,
we'd celebrate New Year's together.

12:34.755 --> 12:37.508
And just like that,
I would grow used to putting it off.

12:37.591 --> 12:41.303
I think in the end,
I'd never be able to return.

12:43.055 --> 12:44.723
Kadono.

12:44.806 --> 12:46.558
If there's a chance,

12:46.642 --> 12:49.394
let's go to the festival
together next time.

12:49.686 --> 12:51.104
Sure.

12:51.188 --> 12:53.106
I'll treat you to something then.

12:53.190 --> 12:55.192
Then I want candy apples.

12:55.275 --> 12:58.153
All right. I'll keep that in mind.

13:24.429 --> 13:26.348
There are so many people!

13:26.723 --> 13:27.891
Ms. Asagao.

13:27.975 --> 13:30.102
It's a pity she couldn't come with us.

13:30.185 --> 13:31.436
But I think

13:31.520 --> 13:35.941
it should be easy for her to move
between heaven and the human world, right?

13:36.608 --> 13:39.820
She was still smiling happily
when she said goodbye.

13:39.903 --> 13:43.073
Master, please don't say
such things carelessly.

13:43.156 --> 13:44.408
What's that?

13:45.200 --> 13:46.034
Ms. Nomari!

13:46.118 --> 13:47.202
- Hey.
- Please wait!

13:47.286 --> 13:48.203
You two.

13:48.287 --> 13:49.872
Be careful not to trip.

13:52.833 --> 13:54.209
In the end,

13:54.293 --> 13:57.296
the legend of the Mirror of Sky Fox
is almost entirely true.

13:57.838 --> 13:59.548
Then, Mr. Kunieda,

13:59.631 --> 14:00.966
what do you mean by "falsehood"?

14:02.551 --> 14:04.178
The Mirror of Sky Fox

14:04.261 --> 14:06.930
is a celestial maiden legend
passed down in Sanjo, Kyoto.

14:07.014 --> 14:10.058
But please think about it.

14:10.142 --> 14:12.144
Since it's a story handed down in Kyoto,

14:12.227 --> 14:16.231
why is the young man in the story
from a sword-making village?

14:17.691 --> 14:18.817
That's right.

14:18.901 --> 14:22.029
In the first place, the Mirror of Sky Fox
and the legend of the feathered robe

14:22.112 --> 14:23.697
were separate stories.

14:23.780 --> 14:28.243
If that's the case, the Mirror of Sky Fox
wasn't made in Kyoto either?

14:28.869 --> 14:30.829
That's right.

14:30.913 --> 14:33.874
Then what about the legend
of the celestial maiden's descent?

14:39.505 --> 14:41.423
Please enjoy, Mr. Jinya.

14:42.799 --> 14:46.261
You've always loved isobe mochi,
haven't you?

14:49.223 --> 14:51.558
My wife will explain the rest.

14:51.642 --> 14:56.021
She knows more
about the Mirror of Sky Fox than I do.

14:56.104 --> 15:00.108
After all, it came from her hometown.

15:02.986 --> 15:04.821
Please allow me to sit next to you.

15:07.574 --> 15:10.661
You want to ask about
the Mirror of Sky Fox, right?

15:15.207 --> 15:18.544
Long ago, the blacksmith
who forged the Mirror of Sky Fox

15:18.627 --> 15:21.839
fused the spear of a female demon
who could foresee the future

15:21.922 --> 15:23.841
with the remnants of her demon blood,

15:23.924 --> 15:25.425
thus creating this mirror.

15:26.134 --> 15:27.135
Demon...

15:27.761 --> 15:28.846
It seems the blacksmith

15:28.929 --> 15:33.475
had originally wanted to make a mirror
that could reflect the future.

15:33.559 --> 15:36.687
But for some reason,
it became a splendid artifact

15:36.770 --> 15:39.815
that could link the past and the future.

15:40.357 --> 15:43.944
That's why it was enshrined
in the shrine as a goshintai,

15:44.027 --> 15:46.989
kept out of the public's reach.

15:47.573 --> 15:50.200
Later, it intertwined
with the legend of the feathered robe,

15:50.284 --> 15:54.329
and people call it the mirror
that connects heaven and earth.

15:54.413 --> 15:59.501
But to be precise, perhaps we're only
calling it that out of wishful thinking.

15:59.918 --> 16:02.254
I didn't know such a thing existed.

16:02.337 --> 16:03.881
Then Asagao...

16:04.298 --> 16:06.800
I think she most likely
came from the future.

16:07.301 --> 16:09.219
I see.

16:12.514 --> 16:15.058
Thank you for telling me, Madam Chiyo.

16:15.434 --> 16:16.476
Well...

16:16.560 --> 16:17.811
Mr. Jinya.

16:17.895 --> 16:22.232
Could you drop the honorifics
and talk to me like you usually do?

16:22.524 --> 16:23.442
What?

16:23.525 --> 16:25.777
To be addressed so formally by Mr. Jinya

16:25.861 --> 16:28.363
feels a little strange.

16:28.447 --> 16:30.407
If you don't mind, could I ask you

16:30.490 --> 16:32.784
to drop the formality
and just call me by my name?

16:32.868 --> 16:35.078
No, I don't think that's appropriate...

16:35.162 --> 16:37.623
Please.

16:38.832 --> 16:40.542
All right.

16:40.626 --> 16:42.503
You should speak casually too, Chiyo.

16:42.878 --> 16:44.129
You're right.

16:44.213 --> 16:45.172
In that case...

16:46.089 --> 16:49.760
can I call you Jinta?

16:56.266 --> 16:58.352
Are you Chitose?

17:00.020 --> 17:03.565
You finally recognize me, Jinta.

17:03.774 --> 17:06.026
Why are you here?

17:06.109 --> 17:09.321
This is the branch
of the shrine in Kadono.

17:09.404 --> 17:11.323
After Lady Itsukihime passed away,

17:11.406 --> 17:14.159
I took over the duties of the Itsukihime.

17:14.243 --> 17:18.372
That's why my husband and I
are in charge of this branch shrine.

17:18.455 --> 17:21.166
You became Itsukihime?

17:21.250 --> 17:22.251
I see.

17:22.334 --> 17:24.127
That's why Chitose became Chiyo.

17:26.421 --> 17:29.925
Who took over
as the current Itsukihime at Kadono?

17:30.008 --> 17:32.344
I've already passed it on to my daughter.

17:32.427 --> 17:36.431
The Itsukihime now doesn't have
to live confined within the shrine.

17:36.515 --> 17:39.685
That Itsukihime's shrine
is just like any other shrine.

17:39.768 --> 17:41.103
As for the name,

17:42.604 --> 17:44.773
it has a beautiful ring to it.

17:54.825 --> 17:58.495
This way,
I suppose I've fulfilled my promise.

17:59.830 --> 18:01.915
I see.

18:05.085 --> 18:07.421
So you've been...

18:09.298 --> 18:10.632
Well then, please have some.

18:11.133 --> 18:12.801
Thank you, I won't be shy.

18:16.680 --> 18:17.806
It's delicious.

18:17.890 --> 18:19.016
Of course.

18:23.562 --> 18:25.063
Father!

18:27.900 --> 18:29.610
Please go.

18:29.693 --> 18:31.028
You're right.

18:32.654 --> 18:33.488
Well then...

18:33.572 --> 18:35.490
No, let's meet another day,

18:35.574 --> 18:36.575
Chitose.

18:36.867 --> 18:38.911
Okay, Jinta.

18:46.376 --> 18:48.879
Father, are you done?

18:48.962 --> 18:49.963
Yes.

18:51.256 --> 18:52.799
I want to eat something.

18:52.883 --> 18:56.845
I see. Do you want to try candy apples?

18:56.929 --> 18:58.972
What are candy apples?

18:59.056 --> 19:00.641
I'm not sure either.

19:03.143 --> 19:06.104
Asagao seems to like them...

19:12.069 --> 19:14.154
Sorry, forget what I said.

19:14.905 --> 19:16.907
Anyway, let's take a look around.

19:16.990 --> 19:18.075
Okay!

19:20.244 --> 19:22.788
I saw a fox just now.

19:22.871 --> 19:24.998
Oh, that? That's...

19:36.510 --> 19:39.471
(Jinta Shrine)

19:42.850 --> 19:45.185
That's strange...

19:58.782 --> 20:01.243
(Frankfurters - Goldfish Scooping)

20:01.340 --> 20:03.240
(Shooting)

20:06.707 --> 20:08.166
Hey, Kaoru?

20:08.876 --> 20:10.294
Are you here for the festival too?

20:10.377 --> 20:12.588
Yes, just looking around a bit.

20:12.880 --> 20:14.339
By the way, Miyaka,

20:14.423 --> 20:16.175
what year is it this year?

20:16.258 --> 20:19.303
Huh? Heisei 21, of course.

20:20.304 --> 20:22.931
I'm really back.

20:23.515 --> 20:26.727
By the way,
that guy was wearing a simple kimono,

20:26.810 --> 20:28.562
looking like he was going on a date.

20:28.645 --> 20:29.688
A date?

20:29.980 --> 20:32.191
He said it's a long-standing promise,

20:32.274 --> 20:34.651
and even said she's a celestial maiden.

20:36.069 --> 20:38.739
I just saw him at the foot
of the stone steps...

20:38.822 --> 20:39.656
Hey, wait--

20:39.740 --> 20:40.949
Kaoru.

20:43.070 --> 20:45.040
(Chocolate Banana)

20:58.675 --> 21:00.677
You're late, Azusaya.

21:02.012 --> 21:05.098
Well...

21:05.599 --> 21:07.351
Catch your breath first.

21:07.434 --> 21:10.479
Okay. I'm sorry.

21:11.813 --> 21:13.857
Well, we...

21:13.941 --> 21:16.652
Um... Long time no see?

21:17.819 --> 21:20.364
It has indeed been a long time.

21:20.447 --> 21:22.449
Now I can call your name
without holding back.

21:22.991 --> 21:24.117
Asagao.

21:26.662 --> 21:29.331
You still remember?

21:29.790 --> 21:32.793
Weren't you the one who wanted
to go to the festival with me?

21:34.628 --> 21:36.755
That's true.

21:36.839 --> 21:39.675
But I didn't expect you to remember.

21:39.758 --> 21:43.345
After all, it was a hundred years ago.

21:44.972 --> 21:47.641
It feels surreal.

21:48.058 --> 21:49.810
That was a nostalgic time for me.

21:50.310 --> 21:53.480
Though I rarely think of it now,

21:54.314 --> 21:56.608
I felt very content during those days.

21:59.611 --> 22:01.572
Hey, Kadono.

22:01.655 --> 22:03.866
There's something I want to ask you.

22:03.949 --> 22:05.117
Can I?

22:05.951 --> 22:06.952
Go ahead.

22:07.578 --> 22:08.996
Thank you.

22:09.913 --> 22:11.290
I want to ask...

22:13.584 --> 22:17.337
Kadono, are you happy now?

22:23.343 --> 22:24.720
That goes without saying.

22:25.804 --> 22:28.891
When you live long enough, the things
you lose naturally grow in number.

22:28.974 --> 22:31.476
Loneliness is inevitable,

22:31.560 --> 22:33.353
but it isn't all bad.

22:34.313 --> 22:38.317
As the things you lose increase,
so will the things you gain.

22:38.400 --> 22:39.693
Besides,

22:40.944 --> 22:42.905
it's precisely because
you've lived long enough

22:42.988 --> 22:46.992
that you can't help but feel thrilled
about an unexpected reunion.

22:47.451 --> 22:52.539
Uh, what you said...
could you be talking about me?

22:53.165 --> 22:55.501
You probably wouldn't understand.

22:56.251 --> 22:58.420
How happy I was

22:58.504 --> 23:00.631
to see you again.

23:01.215 --> 23:04.760
Jeez, there you go again.

23:05.844 --> 23:08.222
Come on, let's go check it out.

23:08.305 --> 23:11.600
As promised,
I'll treat you to candy apples.

23:14.019 --> 23:15.020
Okay!

23:21.568 --> 23:22.569
Mm?

23:26.156 --> 23:30.244
As I thought, that morning-glory
patterned yukata really suits you.

23:30.827 --> 23:34.039
You look just like
a celestial maiden I once saw.
